WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.850
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.400
"Do not attempt."

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.120
That means, uh...

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.450
D-Do—

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.430
Don't copy me.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:12.730
I am not!

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.140
No, that's what it means.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.840
It's an imperative.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.440
Thanks.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.030
You're welcome!

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.350
Jeez! I don't know this!

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.460
Hey, stop checking the answers right away!

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.840
You won't learn anything.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:29.960
You're right.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.940
"It's okay. It's garbage, anyway." 
Constantinople falls.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.380
"How long will mankind fight?" 
The War of the Roses.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.060
"What fast runners they are."

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.790
How do they run so fast?

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.790
<i>October.</i>

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.460
<i>The culture fair is getting close.</i>

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.010
<i>But a big wall separates us and the fair.</i>

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.570
<i>That's right. Midterms.</i>

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.670
<i>To be honest, I'm pretty spooked.</i>

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.580
<i>I have less time for studying than the others.</i>

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.940
<i>But I can't let that beat me.</i>

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:01.990
<i>I...</i>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.460
<i>I will become a local government official!</i>

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:41.930
<b>Twenty-first Haunting 
It Isn't a Manga!</b>

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.840
Let's eat!

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.780
It's been so long since we've had 
Kinzanji miso and fried fish.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.920
Perfect for this time of year!

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.090
I'm so glad I'm Japanese!

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.830
This is amazing!

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.630
I could just eat forever.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.380
Yeah, that's right—

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.770
Hase, what are you doing here?

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.210
Am I not allowed here?

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.770
No, but...

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.410
Tonight, I'm staying here.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.580
Let's have lots of fun, Kuri!

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:11.620
This is so relaxing...

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.090
Hey, Antiquary.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.710
Have anything interesting lately?

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.390
I do, but...

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.670
You do! What do you have?

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.370
What? Stop building it up and show us.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:31.150
Well, I suppose it's fine.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.010
<i>What's fine?</i>

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.700
A lamp?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.190
What is this?

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.850
Put simply,

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.380
it's an omnidirectional 3D projector.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.090
A 3D projector?

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.400
Omnidirectional?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.260
Yes.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.410
Akine-chan, can you erect a 
barrier around the living room?

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.360
Why?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.600
Are you going to do something dangerous?

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.840
No, no.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.630
Just in case, okay?

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.210
<i>It's probably dangerous.</i>

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.550
Oh, fine...

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.570
Um...

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.090
I have to study.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:12.790
Don't worry. It won't take long.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.980
In the real world, less than twenty minutes.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.910
And it's something you might 
only see once in a century.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.900
If you don't, you'll regret it.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.900
Right...

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.330
Everyone gathered here,

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.360
it is time.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.700
Stop building it up.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.780
Do it quickly!

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:34.990
What you'll see tonight is something amazing.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:37.400
Don't let it blow your minds.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.800
Looks like some kind of chip...

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.210
We're floating!

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.390
How scary!

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.560
It's like we're riding in an invisible plane.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.820
It's so pretty!

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:58.900
How wonderful!

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.580
This is great.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.570
Worth living a long time, huh?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.470
I...

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.770
I've never seen a 3D projection like this!

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:07.740
How does it work?

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.120
We aren't in our world.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.620
We aren't?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.230
A dinosaur!

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:17.500
A roc bird!

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.800
That scared me...

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:30.830
Wow!

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.330
So shiny! Like a fairy castle!

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.860
Looks like H.R. Giger.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:49.480
Scales?!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.660
Is that... alive?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.080
A fish that lives in a sea of sand.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:58.220
Then this is a sea?

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.160
A-Amazing.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:07.560
<i>What's really amazing is that it isn't CG.</i>

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:09.820
<i>It isn't Heaven or Hell.</i>

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.830
<i>Worlds like this really exist!</i>

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.880
A Kimon Tonkou barrier?

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.950
Well done, miss.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:33.060
No! My barrier was destroyed?

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.120
And so easily?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.410
Wh-Who is this guy?

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:45.510
Now, I'll do this quickly.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.580
What's wrong, Kuri?

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:51.960
This is bad...

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.180
I don't know what's happening, but it's bad!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.830
Please stop it, master!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.990
Even a billion of you could not beat him.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:03.220
So please don't!

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.570
Thunder spirit! Ithaqua!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.120
Would you stop, please?

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:35.220
Otherwise, I will have to remove this.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:39.960
Wouldn't that be a problem for both of us?

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.730
Are you threatening me?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.900
As expected of the Heretic of the 
Far Reaches. You've got guts.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.260
Quiet...

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:52.390
I'm merely an ordinary antiquary. 
Nothing less and nothing more.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:57.330
But I cannot return empty-handed.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.660
You insist?

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.910
Yes, in the name of truth and God.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.120
Oh, dear.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.700
A-Antiquary?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.160
Farewell, Yushi-kun.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.960
Work hard in your life.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.380
Antiquary!

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.010
Just kidding.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:17.190
Let us meet again, everyone!

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:28.400
Antiquary?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.630
What was that?

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.430
Congresso Vietato.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.360
The miracle hunters.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:43.220
Miracle hunters?

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:47.160
I see. He was an agent for the Secret Church.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.650
I get it.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.070
The Secret... Church?

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.100
They aren't normal priests.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:58.270
They deal directly with exorcisms, spirit 
summoning, ghosts, and monsters.

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:00.220
Stuff the church does secretly.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.740
It's like a manga.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.360
You may not believe it,

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:07.510
but there are many government-run 
special agencies like this.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:10.120
And the Secret Church leads them all.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.180
Just as America calls itself 
the world's policeman,

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:17.920
the Secret Church wants you to think 
it protects the world's spiritual side.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:21.810
The Congresso Vietato is one 
of their special agencies.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:23.950
They go around and collect

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:28.600
things that might create "miracles" 
that would deceive the masses.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:32.010
Looks like they were after the Antiquary.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:36.190
That's why he told me to put up 
a barrier. Not that it worked.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.410
That was cool, though—

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.620
Wait.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:44.020
Then what will happen to the Antiquary?

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:46.590
You really think they'll catch him so easily?

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.390
Nothing to worry about.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:49.340
But...

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.640
They caught me once, too.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.490
I was forced to take lessons
in the morning and at night,

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.830
and do three months of volunteer work.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.380
That was rough!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.440
Four hundred years ago, 
it probably would've been...

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.970
But not now.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.790
My heart's still pounding.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.490
I couldn't get any studying done.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.670
That sucks.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:28.750
The world's so big...

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:30.950
Flying dinosaurs.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.240
Fish the size of castles.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.230
And now, a Secret Church?

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.900
How far am I supposed to go?

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:40.850
As far as you can, right?

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:42.480
Don't make it sound so easy.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.700
If I make it sound hard, it's still the same.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.160
Things happen that not even the

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.880
amazing people in this building can predict.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.150
The world is filled with threats.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.290
Yeah.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:57.610
<i>Yes.</i>

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:59.440
<i>I'm sure a world</i>

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.280
<i>that's filled with threats 
is still waiting for me.</i>

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:18.550
I did it!

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:24.810
You did not.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.770
"Apologize" is an intransitive verb,

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:31.600
so you need "to" before the object, "him."

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:32.940
I see.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:36.050
You came all the way here because you said

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.330
you couldn't concentrate in the apartment.

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.020
Work a little harder.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.650
Yeah... I need to work harder.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:47.780
I'm just a high school student, 
not a genius like you.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.380
I'm not a genius.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:54.100
I simply remember every single 
thing I hear in class.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:55.600
So you really are a genius!

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.290
If I have to, I'll stay with you all day.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.790
Get ready.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:01.970
Hase!

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.470
Perfect chance for a photo!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.020
T-Tashiro, you...

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:10.210
I see! I knew it!

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:12.330
He's just an old friend!

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:14.630
He's just tutoring me!

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.980
Oh, really?

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:21.150
Wh-What?

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:25.780
Hello. I've known Inaba since third grade.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.320
My name is Mizuki Hase.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.330
I'm Inaba's classmate, Takako Tashiro!

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:37.630
Right now, I can offer you the latest 
top-secret information on Inaba for super cheap.

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:39.070
That sounds great.

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:40.240
W-Wait!

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:49.430
<b></b>

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.010
What's "the latest top-secret information"?

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.700
Hase, don't start swapping 
contact info with Tashiro!

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:46.890
What are you showing each other?!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.430
Sir, please be quiet in the restaurant.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:51.530
<i>I'm tired...</i>

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.200
<i>Really tired.</i>

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.850
She had a lot of energy.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.890
Yeah, but...

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.560
Good luck with your tests, Inaba.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.550
Yeah. Thanks for coming today.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:11.910
I'm back.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.330
Welcome back, Yushi-kun!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.610
My package finally arrived.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:21.650
I have something that will 
be very useful for you.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:22.710
Useful?

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.450
Everyone's waiting.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.900
Fujiyuki-sensei!

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.560
Hello, there.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.950
Is this another event for the hospital?

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.490
I'm here to do an appraisal.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.320
An appraisal?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:51.780
Of that.

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:53.990
God of the Moon, Soma.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.170
The elixir of immortality, Amrita.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.940
The elixir of immortality?

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.810
It makes you super energetic!

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:04.060
You can stay up all night and study!

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:05.290
Doctor...

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:08.110
Well, he isn't entirely wrong, 
but that's mostly fantasy.

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:09.980
Hey, don't say that!

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.720
Getting this was really hard!

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.260
This is found in the middle of the 
middle of the middle of nowhere.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.350
My car broke down, the jungle was endless,

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.630
and my rubber boat sprang a leak!

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.270
Take care of your crap!

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:25.190
And when I finally reached the village,

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.440
the guy who knew about Amrita was long dead.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:33.280
And only a shady old lady who'd heard 
a legend knew anything at all.

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.220
Amrita...

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:38.040
I think I may have heard of it.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.340
I was so disappointed.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:47.230
But I thought to myself, "A man's true 
worth is tested when things are bad!"

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:48.950
Cheers!

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:52.420
Hey!

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.480
I think I like this stuff better.

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.350
We're listening.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:16:00.640
Ruriko-san, I'll take some salt-baked tuna!

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:05.690
But I did my best to get her to remember!

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:06.820
And...

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:10.040
You're so nice.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.350
I think it was around here.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.790
I think this will do.

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:18.770
Stingy as hell, those Indians!

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:22.160
No eternal romance or glories 
of the gods for them, huh?

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.160
I ended up paying ten times the average 
annual salary for an Indian.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.840
So, is it really authentic?

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.580
That's why Fujiyuki-sensei is here.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.510
I wanted him to look.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:35.350
All right.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.850
<i>What language is this?</i>

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:03.740
Letters... Letters cast by light!

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.580
The history of this elixir.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.630
Elixir?

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:10.680
This magic circle can read an item's history.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.940
Read... its history?

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.300
It's called object reading.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.780
Fujiyuki-sensei's power is an 
even more amazing version.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:22.220
He can read it in 3D.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.600
<i>Read letters in 3D?</i>

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.630
<i>I have no idea.</i>

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:28.900
<i>But...</i>

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.830
<i>Fujiyuki-sensei is kind of cool!</i>

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.040
It seems it's real.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.490
The real elixir of immortality?!

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.150
I wouldn't say immortality,

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:45.400
but a powerful, life-extending 
magic has been cast on it.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.750
The longest-lived person to take 
it lived eight hundred years.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:50.170
Eight hundred years?

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:53.920
Like Yaobikuni, who ate mermaid flesh!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.690
Eight hundred years is close enough 
to immortality for me.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.260
It was the old woman you met.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.220
She took the elixir 
from its rightful place.

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:07.320
She was once a priestess at a temple of Soma.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:12.280
Its original holder entrusted it to 
her, so it would not be misused.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:14.280
Just like Yaobikuni.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:21.620
The priestess protected the elixir of eternal
life from evil and wandered across the land,

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.950
using it to help people.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:28.110
The elixir also had the power to heal.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:31.720
Sometimes, she would sell a single drop,

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.840
and use it to help others.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:38.000
And one of those legends
made it into the world, huh?

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:43.230
Years passed, and people no longer 
believed in the legend of Amrita.

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:47.060
And at last, she was able to find peace.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:52.920
So when someone visited her, 
she would toy with them.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.660
And it seems...

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.360
Nothing is left inside.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:18:59.920
It isn't?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.080
Over eight hundred years, 
she must have used it all.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:06.110
But it was definitely kept in this vessel.

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:07.520
No way!

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.630
It's empty! Empty!

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:14.510
It appears the Soma priestess
pulled one over on you.

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:16.550
That...

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:20.190
Is this really worth so much?

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:23.250
Then give me some money for it.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:24.970
That stupid old woman!

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.000
I see.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:31.470
For years, she's sold empty 
vessels like that.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:33.150
Even if they were empty,

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.440
people would just give up and 
think the legend only a story.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.400
That was what she took advantage of.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.150
Pretty smart.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:44.030
She didn't waste those eight 
hundred years, huh?

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.470
A learning experience. Right, Furuhonya-san?

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:47.540
Damn it all!

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.040
Amrita...

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:03.710
It's real.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.990
Think your lifespan got longer?

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:26.740
Yeah. By about seven months?

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:34.000
Who cares about seven months?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.060
Oh, what is this?

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.460
The elixir of immortality. Amrita.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:42.420
It's empty, so Furuhonya-san gave it to me.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:46.010
But there may still be a drop or so left.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:48.910
That's amazing, though.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.700
Living eight hundred years.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:54.350
But immortality is impossible for humans.

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:56.020
I'm sure.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:03.430
A finite life and an infinite world, huh?

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:04.610
Master?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.190
How will I live my life?

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:11.020
Well, it doesn't matter. 
I know what I want to do.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:12.950
First goal! Work for the prefecture!

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.510
Second goal, be a businessman 
at a strict company!

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:16.580
Let's do this!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.770
Don't forget the path to becoming a mage.

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:19.820
Right, right.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:22.350
First, I need to finish studying...

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:23.570
Let's go!

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:32.500
Look at that cute face, chirp.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.740
He looks so happy, chirp.

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:36.130
He must be having a great dream, chirp!

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.900
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:23:11.230 --> 00:23:13.740
In negotiations, the first 
moment is very important.

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:16.620
Everything depends on your 
advantage over your opponent.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:19.370
Wow, Hase... You must never lose!

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:22.630
Compared to my dad and older 
sister, I have a lot to learn.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.120
Just you wait! I'll show them!

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:28.080
So life's tough for you, too?

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:31.090
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:32.630
Burning Student Assembly!

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.050
<b>Twenty-second Haunting 
Burning Student Assembly!</b>

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:36.100
A historic moment for JTB is about to begin.
